WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A network written out as a list of edges is complete, but it is not readable. A language model has to recover the structure before it can answer anything about it.

2
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:27.000
BioGlyph starts by retrieving the region around the nodes in the question. Everything after this is computed on that region, never on the whole network.

3
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:41.648
Classical algorithms do the arithmetic. Degree, betweenness, k core, articulation points, bridges and communities, computed exactly, with nothing learned.

4
00:00:41.648 --> 00:00:56.648
One fixed rule then assigns each of eleven structural roles. A node whose removal splits its component is a cut node, and the algorithm decides that, not the model.

5
00:00:56.648 --> 00:01:12.648
Every role carries the measurements that triggered it and what would happen if that part were removed. That last clause is exactly what a table of numbers leaves out.

6
00:01:12.648 --> 00:01:30.176
A frozen open model reading these descriptions answers seventy point six percent of benchmark questions correctly. Reading the identical measurements as a table it manages thirty nine point five percent, which is worse than showing it no graph at all.

7
00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:47.128
The same roles carry biological meaning. In the budding yeast interactome, cross community connectors are essential fifty seven point six percent of the time against a background of thirty point nine, with the labels withheld from the compiler.
